[{"order":1,"type":"heading","text":"Advanced Android UI: Custom Layouts, Modifiers, and Canvas Drawing in Jetpack Compose"},{"order":2,"type":"paragraph","text":"Jetpack Compose provides a powerful declarative UI model. However, when standard components fall short, developers must drop down to custom layouts, write custom modifiers, or draw directly onto the Canvas. This tutorial explores these advanced concepts in Kotlin."},{"order":3,"type":"heading","text":"1. Writing Custom Modifiers"},{"order":4,"type":"paragraph","text":"Modifiers allow you to decorate or augment a composable. You can create custom modifiers using the modifier factory functions and the ModifierNodeElement API for high-performance state handling."},{"order":5,"type":"code","text":"fun Modifier.debugBorder(color: Color) = this.then(
    Modifier.drawBehind {
        drawRect(color = color, style = Stroke(width = 2.dp.toPx()))
    }
)"},{"order":6,"type":"heading","text":"2. Creating Custom Layouts"},{"order":7,"type":"paragraph","text":"When Row, Column, and Box are not enough, the Layout composable lets you measure and position children manually. Every layout must measure its children before determining its own size."},{"order":8,"type":"code","text":"@Composable
fun CascadingLayout(
    modifier: Modifier = Modifier,
    content: @Composable () -> Unit
) {
    Layout(
        modifier = modifier,
        content = content
    ) { measurables, constraints ->
        val placeables = measurables.map { it.measure(constraints) }

        layout(constraints.maxWidth, constraints.maxHeight) {
            var xCoord = 0
            var yCoord = 0
            placeables.forEach { placeable ->
                placeable.placeRelative(x = xCoord, y = yCoord)
                xCoord += 50
                yCoord += 50
            }
        }
    }
}"},{"order":9,"type":"heading","text":"3. Direct Canvas Drawing"},{"order":10,"type":"paragraph","text":"The Canvas composable provides a scoped DrawScope where you can execute 2D graphics commands. It is ideal for data visualization, custom progress bars, and game rendering."},{"order":11,"type":"code","text":"@Composable
fun PulsingCircleCanvas(color: Color) {
    Canvas(modifier = Modifier.size(100.dp)) {
        val radius = size.minDimension / 2
        drawCircle(
            color = color,
            radius = radius,
            center = center
        )
    }
}"},{"order":12,"type":"heading","text":"Best Practices for Advanced Compose UI"},{"order":13,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Avoid heavy allocations inside the draw phase to prevent jank during animations."},{"order":14,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Prefer ModifierNodeElement over factory extensions for modifiers that hold state."},{"order":15,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Always respect incoming constraints in custom layouts to maintain layout predictability."}]
